From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 01:11:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web-app: enlarge chat navbar button click targets

The chat title-bar icon buttons (apps, map, three-dot menu) had a 20x20px
click target sitting in a 50px-tall navbar with a 12px dead gap between
them, so most of the bar was unclickable. Grow each button's hit box to
fill the vertical dead space and the inter-button gap, and cancel the
growth with negative margins so the icons and navbar height stay
pixel-for-pixel identical.

Rebased onto v2.62.0: upstream turned the navbar buttons into
IconButtons with a CSS-module .navbarButton class and 22x22 icons
(f7da2748c, #6527) and grouped the last-used apps in an .appsGroup with
a 10px gap (69712ef3b, #6572). The hit box is now 32x40 around the 22px
icon (5px per side, so neighbouring boxes never overlap, also inside
.appsGroup); the #three-dot-menu-button override is gone with
upstream's.
---
 .../components/ChatView/styles.module.scss    | 24 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/frontend/src/components/ChatView/styles.module.scss b/packages/frontend/src/components/ChatView/styles.module.scss
index cf744af0e47ddd3ed7ff7e894e48389da456cca8..6afb3c1276295deaf686cf0feb09e0deaac6b7e0 100644
--- a/packages/frontend/src/components/ChatView/styles.module.scss
+++ b/packages/frontend/src/components/ChatView/styles.module.scss
@@ -60,12 +60,27 @@
       min-height: 26px;
     }
 
+    // Enlarge the click target without changing anything visible: the icon
+    // stays centered in a bigger box and negative margins cancel out the
+    // added size, so icon positions and the navbar height are pixel-for-pixel
+    // identical to before. Previously the box was only 22x22 inside a 50px
+    // navbar, with a 12px (dead, unclickable) gap between buttons.
+    $icon-size: 22px;
+    $hit-width: 32px; // reclaims the inter-button gap (5px each side)
+    $hit-height: 40px; // reclaims the 50px navbar's vertical dead space
+    // half the growth, given back on each side
+    $hit-shift: calc((#{$icon-size} - #{$hit-width}) / 2);
+
     .navbarButton {
       padding: 0;
-      width: 22px;
-      height: 22px;
+      width: $hit-width;
+      height: $hit-height;
       border-radius: 0;
-      margin-inline-end: 12px;
+      // Keep the icon exactly where it was and the row footprint unchanged:
+      // shift the wider box back by half the growth, and shrink the trailing
+      // gap by the same amount (12px stays the icon-to-icon spacing).
+      margin-inline-start: $hit-shift;
+      margin-inline-end: calc(12px + #{$hit-shift});
       align-items: center;
       justify-content: center;
       &:hover {
@@ -80,7 +95,8 @@
       margin-inline-end: 24px;
 
       .navbarButton {
-        margin-inline-end: 0;
+        // the group's gap is the icon-to-icon spacing here
+        margin-inline-end: $hit-shift;
       }
     }
 
